#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""What a build's frame costs on this machine's GPU. Usage:

    tools/bench <build> [--size WxH] [--frames A-B] [--runs N] [--rest S] [--against <build2>]
                [--passes-build P] [--against-passes-build P2] [--no-passes]
                [--canary LABEL [--canary-share P]] [--json FILE] [--host PATH] [--timeout S]
                [-- <more wrela-host flags>]

Every launch goes through tools/gpu (the guard, the machine's one GPU lock, the timeout) at --size
(default 3840x2160), frames 0 to B, and frames A to B are read (0-based, as the host numbers them).

THE FRAME'S COST is its span, from runs as a frame really runs: the host's `--timestamps` without
`--serial`, passes overlapped, frames back to back. The host prints `frame N  span X ms` for each
frame: on the GPU's clock, from the start of the frame's first timed pass or dispatch to the end of
its last (toolchain/host/src/gpu.rs, `frame_spans`). It is not wall time, and the CPU's time
between frames is not in it. In this mode the host waits on the CPU after each submission to read
its timestamps, so where a frame is submitted in more than one piece (a pass drawn to the screen
ends, a buffer is read back, a very large upload, the uniform ring fills), the GPU's idle time
while the CPU reads and records the rest is inside the span: a span is never less than the GPU's
work, and can be more. The bench prints the span's median and range over the frames; with several
runs, the median of the runs' medians and the runs' range. A build with a pass labelled `load` (a
heavy pass drawn beside the frame to hold the GPU's clock up) has it inside its span: no host flag
leaves a pass out, and the load is a build setting (`wrela build --set LOAD=...`), so the bench
warns and marks the span; build the span's build without the load, and give the load's build as
--passes-build.

WHERE THE COST IS: one more run of each build with `--timestamps --serial`, each pass and
dispatch alone, timed by its own timestamps: each label's median and range over the frames (a
label counts 0 in a frame it didn't run in, and the table says so), and their sum. These DO NOT
add up to the frame: passes overlap on this GPU, alone each pays its own start and drain, and a
span holds the GPU's idle moments inside a frame (the old opening at 1280x720, frames 300-419,
three runs: 15.2 to 19.5 ms summed, spans of 17.0 to 17.3; in its warm-up, frames 30-149, 24.4
summed). Timed alone, light passes let
the M4 lower its clock (a light frame reads up to 4 times slow), so the pass table wants a `load`
pass beside it, left out of the sum; a pass table without one is warned about.

SETTLING: a scene may warm up for seconds (the old opening: a span of 24 ms for its first 160
frames, 17 ms from frame 240 on). Each span run's window is cut in thirds and the first third's
median compared with the last's; a difference past the noise is warned: still settling, take
later frames. The noise is the larger of five standard errors of the difference (from the median
absolute deviation of the last third) and 15% of the last third: a settled scene's cost still
drifts with what its camera sees, and frame follows frame, so the standard error alone is too
small (the old opening at 1280x720, settled: thirds 5.5% and 10.1% apart, 3.4 and 6.1 standard
errors; windows across its warm-up 20% and 26%, 9 and 21 standard errors). The default window, 300-419, starts 5 s in (at 60 frames a second). A
plateau that ends after the window can't be seen from inside it (the old opening's frames 30-149
read settled, at 24 ms): when a scene is new, run it long once and look.

  --runs N        N span runs (default 1; 3 with --against), --rest S seconds apart (default 30:
                  the M4 is fanless and throttles when hot). One passes run a build in any case.
                  Before each run the bench waits for a quiet machine: other processes under 300%
                  of a core for three samples, up to 600 s (WRELA_BENCH_QUIET_WAIT sets the
                  seconds, 0 for none), then runs anyway and warns as before.
  --against B2    A/B on the span: runs A B A B ..., N pairs. Prints each pair, each side's
                  median and range and B - A, with a verdict: faster or slower when the
                  difference is more than the noise, else inside the noise. The noise is A's
                  spread against itself (its runs' greatest median less its least), or B's where
                  that is wider; it needs --runs 2 or more. The pass tables are shown side by
                  side, with their differences and no verdict (one run each).
  --passes-build P, --against-passes-build P2
                  the build to time passes alone for A (B): the same program built with its load
                  pass on. Default: the build itself.
  --no-passes     no passes run.
  --canary L      a pass that does the same work in every run: warns when its median in the span
                  runs moves by more than --canary-share P percent (default 5) of the least (heat,
                  or the GPU had company).
  --json FILE     everything printed, and each run's per-frame spans, as JSON.
  --host PATH     a wrela-host binary for tools/gpu to run (else tools/gpu's own, built if stale).
  --timeout S     tools/gpu's wall-clock limit for one run (default 600).
  -- ...          more wrela-host flags (--input script.json, say). Not --frames or --size.

RADV on the Linux machine lowers its shader clock to 400 MHz of 1,800 whenever frames leave it idle,
as light scenes' do (the duel at 1920x1080: 35% of a run's samples at 400 MHz; with a load
beside it, 18%), so where amdgpu gives the clock (`pp_dpm_sclk`) it is sampled every 0.05 s while
a run holds the GPU, each run's line says the share at the top level, and a span run under 90%
is warned about (docs/vulkan.md). The M4 lowers its clock too, but says nothing of it.

A span run during heavy CPU work elsewhere reads high (the old opening at 1280x720, frames
300-419: 27.4 ms while another job's tests used 8 cores, 17.2 ms without), so the other
processes' CPU is sampled while a run holds the GPU (`ps`, every 2 s), its median shown on the
run's line, and a span run past 400% of a core (the M4's 4 performance cores) is warned about.

What tools/gpu and the host say besides timings (the wait for the GPU lock, errors) is passed on
to stderr behind `  | `; each run's line says how long it waited and how long it ran.

Exit status: 0; 2 for a usage error; else the failed run's (3: the guard refused the build, 124:
the timeout killed it).
"""

import glob
import json
import math
import os
import re
import statistics
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time

TOOLS = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
# The launcher: tools/gpu. The tests put a fake in its place.
GPU = os.path.join(TOOLS, "gpu")
# Other processes' CPU past this (percent of one core: the M4's 4 performance cores), during a
# span run, is warned about; sampled every SAMPLE_S seconds.
BUSY = 400.0
SAMPLE_S = 2.0
# The GPU's clock, where the machine says it (amdgpu), sampled this often; a span run whose clock
# is at its top level in less than CLOCK_TOP percent of the samples is warned about.
CLOCK_S = 0.05
CLOCK_TOP = 90.0
LOAD = "load"
SUM = "sum of passes alone"
SPAN_NAME = "frame span"

TIMING = re.compile(r"^frame\s+(\d+)\s+(.+?)\s+(-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?) us$")
SPAN = re.compile(r"^frame\s+(\d+)\s+span\s+(-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?) ms$")
WAITED = re.compile(r"^gpu: waited (\d+(?:\.\d+)?) s$")
HASH = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{16}$")

# wrela-host flags the bench sets itself, or that don't time frames.
OWN = {"--frames", "--size", "--until", "--no-gpu", "--replay", "--compare-ticks", "--capture",
       "--timestamps", "--serial"}


class Usage(Exception):
    pass


# ---- reading the host's lines ------------------------------------------------------------------


def read_timings(lines):
    """The host's `--timestamps` lines: {frame: {label: microseconds}}, each label's pieces in a
    frame summed, and the labels in the order first seen. Other lines are ignored."""
    frames, order = {}, []
    for line in lines:
        m = TIMING.match(line.rstrip("\n"))
        if not m:
            continue
        f, label, us = int(m.group(1)), m.group(2), float(m.group(3))
        per = frames.setdefault(f, {})
        per[label] = per.get(label, 0.0) + us
        if label not in order:
            order.append(label)
    return frames, order


def read_spans(lines):
    """The host's `frame N  span X ms` lines: {frame: ms}."""
    spans = {}
    for line in lines:
        m = SPAN.match(line.rstrip("\n"))
        if m:
            spans[int(m.group(1))] = float(m.group(2))
    return spans


def window(spans, first, last):
    """The spans of frames `first`..`last` (inclusive) that the host printed, in frame order."""
    return [spans[f] for f in sorted(spans) if first <= f <= last]


def measure(frames, order, first, last):
    """One run's frames `first`..`last` (inclusive): for each label its time in each frame read
    (ms; 0 in a frame where it didn't run), and each frame's sum of every label but `load`."""
    read = [f for f in sorted(frames) if first <= f <= last]
    labels = {}
    for label in order:
        values = [frames[f].get(label, 0.0) / 1000.0 for f in read]
        ran = sum(1 for f in read if label in frames[f])
        if ran:
            labels[label] = {"values": values, "ran": ran}
    sums = [sum(us for label, us in frames[f].items() if label != LOAD) / 1000.0 for f in read]
    return {"frames": read, "labels": labels, "sums": sums, "load": LOAD in labels}


def spread(values):
    """Median, least and greatest."""
    return {"median": statistics.median(values), "min": min(values), "max": max(values)}


def settling(values):
    """Whether a run's spans have settled: the window's first third's median against its last
    third's. The noise is the larger of 15% of the last third's median and five standard errors
    of that difference, each third's median's from the last third's median absolute deviation
    (a normal's sigma is 1.4826 MADs; a median's standard error 1.2533 sigma / sqrt(n)). None
    for under 15 frames."""
    n = len(values) // 3
    if n < 5:
        return None
    early, late = values[:n], values[-n:]
    a, b = statistics.median(early), statistics.median(late)
    mad = statistics.median(abs(x - b) for x in late)
    noise = max(0.15 * b, 5.0 * math.sqrt(2.0) * 1.2533 * 1.4826 * mad / math.sqrt(n))
    return {"first": a, "last": b, "noise": noise, "settled": abs(a - b) <= noise}


# ---- many runs, and A against B ---------------------------------------------------------------


def summarize(lists):
    """Runs' values (a list a run): the median of the runs' medians, each run's median, the runs'
    range and the frames' range."""
    meds = [statistics.median(v) for v in lists if v]
    every = [x for v in lists for x in v]
    return {"median": statistics.median(meds), "runs": meds, "runs_min": min(meds),
            "runs_max": max(meds), "frames_min": min(every), "frames_max": max(every),
            "frames": len(every)}


def pass_table(m):
    """One passes run's labels and their sum: {label: summary}, labels in order, the sum last."""
    out = {}
    for label, v in m["labels"].items():
        out[label] = dict(summarize([v["values"]]), ran=v["ran"], read=len(m["frames"]))
    out[SUM] = dict(summarize([m["sums"]]), ran=len(m["frames"]), read=len(m["frames"]))
    return out


def verdict(a_runs, b_runs):
    """B against A from each side's run medians: (B - A, the noise, the word). The noise is a
    side's spread against itself (its greatest run median less its least): A's, or B's where
    B's is wider, since a build that reads unsteadily can't be told apart by less. A difference
    no larger than the noise is inside it. With one run a side there is no noise, and no
    verdict."""
    a, b = statistics.median(a_runs), statistics.median(b_runs)
    diff = b - a
    if len(a_runs) < 2 or len(b_runs) < 2:
        return diff, None, "no verdict (one run a side: the noise is unknown)"
    noise = max(max(a_runs) - min(a_runs), max(b_runs) - min(b_runs))
    if abs(diff) <= noise:
        return diff, noise, "inside the noise"
    return diff, noise, "faster" if diff < 0 else "slower"


def canary_check(runs, label, share):
    """Whether the canary held over the span runs: (its run medians, how far they moved as a
    share of the least, a warning or None)."""
    meds = []
    for r in runs:
        values = r["labels"].get(label, {}).get("values")
        if not values:
            return meds, None, f"the canary `{label}` didn't run in every run"
        meds.append(statistics.median(values))
    if len(meds) < 2:
        return meds, 0.0, None
    least = min(meds)
    moved = (max(meds) - least) / least * 100.0 if least > 0 else float("inf")
    if moved > share:
        return meds, moved, (f"the canary `{label}` moved {moved:.1f}% across the runs "
                             f"({least:.3f} to {max(meds):.3f} ms), more than {share:g}%: "
                             "the machine was hot or the GPU had company; rest and rerun")
    return meds, moved, None


# ---- running the host -------------------------------------------------------------------------


def others_cpu(ours):
    """The CPU the machine's other processes use now, in percent of one core (`ps`'s %cpu,
    a short decaying average): every process but this one and those under the pid `ours`."""
    try:
        rows = subprocess.run(["ps", "-A", "-o", "pid=,ppid=,pcpu="], capture_output=True,
                              text=True, timeout=10).stdout.split("\n")
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    procs = {}
    for row in rows:
        parts = row.split()
        if len(parts) == 3:
            try:
                procs[int(parts[0])] = (int(parts[1]), float(parts[2]))
            except ValueError:
                pass
    mine = {os.getpid(), ours}
    grew = True
    while grew:
        grew = False
        for pid, (ppid, _) in procs.items():
            if ppid in mine and pid not in mine:
                mine.add(pid)
                grew = True
    return sum(cpu for pid, (_, cpu) in procs.items() if pid not in mine)


def sclk_file():
    """amdgpu's shader clock levels (Linux: `pp_dpm_sclk`, the level in use marked `*`), or None
    where there's none (the Mac)."""
    for card in sorted(glob.glob("/sys/class/drm/card*/device/pp_dpm_sclk")):
        return card
    return None


def sclk_now(path):
    """(the shader clock now, its top level), in MHz, or None."""
    try:
        levels = open(path).read().split("\n")
    except OSError:
        return None
    mhz = [(int(m.group(1)), "*" in line) for line in levels
           for m in [re.search(r"(\d+)\s*[Mm]hz", line)] if m]
    now = [f for f, star in mhz if star]
    return (now[0], max(f for f, _ in mhz)) if now and mhz else None


QUIET_CPU = 300.0     # others' CPU (percent of a core) under which the machine counts as quiet
QUIET_FOR = 3         # samples in a row under it, two seconds apart
QUIET_WAIT = 600.0    # the longest a run waits for quiet (seconds); WRELA_BENCH_QUIET_WAIT sets it


def wait_quiet():
    """Before a run: waits until the machine's other processes have used less than QUIET_CPU
    for QUIET_FOR samples in a row, or QUIET_WAIT seconds have passed (then it runs anyway, and
    the run's own warning says the CPU was busy). Several builders share this machine: a span
    read while another cooks at 700% of a core is noise, and was being measured again and again.
    Returns the seconds waited."""
    try:
        limit = float(os.environ.get("WRELA_BENCH_QUIET_WAIT", QUIET_WAIT))
    except ValueError:
        limit = QUIET_WAIT
    began, calm, said = time.monotonic(), 0, False
    while limit > 0 and time.monotonic() - began < limit:
        cpu = others_cpu(os.getpid())
        if cpu is None:
            break
        calm = calm + 1 if cpu < QUIET_CPU else 0
        if calm >= QUIET_FOR:
            break
        if not said and calm == 0:
            print(f"bench: waiting for a quiet machine (others' CPU {cpu:.0f}%, "
                  f"up to {limit:g} s)", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
            said = True
        time.sleep(2.0)
    return time.monotonic() - began


class Sampler:
    """Others' CPU every few seconds while a run holds the GPU (not while it waits for the lock);
    and where amdgpu says, the GPU's shader clock every CLOCK_S seconds: RADV's lowers itself to
    400 MHz of 1,800 while light frames leave it idle (docs/vulkan.md, measuring)."""

    def __init__(self, child):
        self.child, self.waiting, self.samples = child, False, []
        self.sclk, self.clocks = sclk_file(), []
        self.done = threading.Event()
        self.thread = threading.Thread(target=self.run, daemon=True)
        self.thread.start()

    def run(self):
        last = time.monotonic()
        while not self.done.wait(CLOCK_S if self.sclk else SAMPLE_S):
            if self.waiting:
                continue
            if self.sclk:
                now = sclk_now(self.sclk)
                if now:
                    self.clocks.append(now)
                if time.monotonic() - last < SAMPLE_S:
                    continue
                last = time.monotonic()
            cpu = others_cpu(self.child.pid)
            if cpu is not None:
                self.samples.append(cpu)

    def top_share(self):
        """The share of the run's clock samples at the clock's top level, in percent, or None."""
        if not self.clocks:
            return None
        return 100.0 * sum(1 for f, top in self.clocks if f >= top) / len(self.clocks)

    def stop(self):
        self.done.set()
        self.thread.join()
        if not self.samples:  # a run shorter than a sample's wait
            cpu = others_cpu(self.child.pid)
            if cpu is not None:
                self.samples.append(cpu)
        return statistics.median(self.samples) if self.samples else None



def run_once(build, size, last, extra, host, timeout, serial):
    """One run of `build` through tools/gpu, frames 0..last, with --timestamps (and --serial).
    Returns (status, the timed lines, state hash, seconds waited for the lock, seconds in all,
    the median of the other processes' CPU while it ran, in percent of a core, or None, and the
    share of its GPU clock samples at the top level, in percent, or None)."""
    cmd = [GPU]
    if host:
        cmd += ["--host", host]
    cmd += ["--timeout", str(timeout), build, "--frames", str(last + 1), "--size", size,
            "--timestamps"] + (["--serial"] if serial else []) + extra
    began = time.monotonic()
    child = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)
    sampler = Sampler(child)
    out = []
    reader = threading.Thread(target=lambda: out.extend(child.stdout), daemon=True)
    reader.start()
    timed, waited = [], 0.0
    for line in child.stderr:
        if TIMING.match(line.rstrip("\n")) or SPAN.match(line.rstrip("\n")):
            timed.append(line)
            continue
        m = WAITED.match(line.strip())
        if m:
            waited += float(m.group(1))
        if line.startswith("gpu: waiting for the GPU"):
            sampler.waiting = True
        if line.startswith("gpu: waited"):
            sampler.waiting = False
            sampler.samples.clear()
        if line.startswith("gpu: guard: largest"):
            continue
        sys.stderr.write("  | " + line)
        sys.stderr.flush()
    status = child.wait()
    busy = sampler.stop()
    top = sampler.top_share()
    reader.join()
    for line in out:
        if not HASH.match(line.strip()):
            sys.stderr.write("  | " + line)
    hashes = [line.strip() for line in out if HASH.match(line.strip())]
    return (status, timed, (hashes[-1] if hashes else None), waited, time.monotonic() - began,
            busy, top)


# ---- printing ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------


def warn(lines, warnings):
    bar = "bench: WARNING " + "-" * 60
    print(bar, file=sys.stderr)
    for line in lines:
        print(f"bench: WARNING  {line}", file=sys.stderr)
    print(bar, file=sys.stderr)
    warnings.append(" ".join(lines))


def no_load_warning(build, warnings):
    warn([f"{build}'s passes were timed alone with no `{LOAD}` pass beside them.",
          "The M4 lowers its GPU clock under a light load, and a light pass timed alone reads",
          "up to 4 times slow: the pass table may be the clock's, not the work's. Give a",
          f"build drawing a heavy pass labelled `{LOAD}` as --passes-build (docs/dead-ends.md,",
          "\"Measuring\"). The frame's span is not affected."], warnings)


def load_in_span_warning(build, warnings):
    warn([f"{build} draws a `{LOAD}` pass: the frame's span INCLUDES it.",
          "No host flag leaves a pass out; build the program without its load for the span",
          "and give the load's build as --passes-build."], warnings)


def fmt_range(lo, hi):
    return f"[{lo:.3f}, {hi:.3f}]"


def pct(diff, base):
    return f"{diff / base * 100.0:+.1f}%" if base else "n/a"


PASSES_TITLE = ("where the cost is: passes timed alone (--serial){load}; "
                "these do not add up to the frame")


def print_passes(table, loaded):
    print(PASSES_TITLE.format(load=", a load beside them" if loaded else ", NO load beside them"))
    names = [k for k in table if k != SUM]
    width = max(len(k) for k in list(table) + [f"{LOAD} (left out)", f"{SUM} (not the frame)"]) + 2
    head = f"{'':<{width}}{'median':>9}  frames"
    print(head)
    for k in names + [SUM]:
        s = table[k]
        name = f"{LOAD} (left out)" if k == LOAD else k
        if k == SUM:
            print("-" * len(head))
            name = f"{SUM} (not the frame)"
        row = f"{name:<{width}}{s['median']:>9.3f}  {fmt_range(s['frames_min'], s['frames_max'])}"
        if s["ran"] < s["read"]:
            row += f"  ran in {s['ran']} of {s['read']} frames (0 in the others)"
        print(row)


def print_passes_ab(ta, tb, la, lb):
    print(PASSES_TITLE.format(load=(", a load beside them" if la and lb else
                                    ", NO load beside them" if not la and not lb else
                                    f", a load beside {'A' if la else 'B'} only")))
    names = [k for k in ta if k != SUM] + [k for k in tb if k not in ta and k != SUM]
    width = max(len(k) for k in names + [f"{SUM} (not the frame)", f"{LOAD} (left out)"]) + 2
    head = f"{'':<{width}}{'A':>9}  {'B':>9}  {'B - A':>18}"
    print(head)
    for k in names + [SUM]:
        name = f"{LOAD} (left out)" if k == LOAD else k
        if k == SUM:
            print("-" * len(head))
            name = f"{SUM} (not the frame)"
        a = ta[k]["median"] if k in ta else None
        b = tb[k]["median"] if k in tb else None
        if a is None or b is None:
            print(f"{name:<{width}}only in {'A' if b is None else 'B'}: {(a if b is None else b):.3f}")
            continue
        print(f"{name:<{width}}{a:>9.3f}  {b:>9.3f}  {b - a:>+9.3f} ({pct(b - a, a):>6})")


# ---- the command -------------------------------------------------------------------------------


def parse_args(argv):
    o = {"build": None, "size": "3840x2160", "frames": (300, 419), "runs": None, "rest": 30.0,
         "against": None, "passes_build": None, "against_passes_build": None, "passes": True,
         "canary": None, "share": 5.0, "json": None, "host": None, "timeout": 600.0, "extra": []}
    if "--" in argv:
        i = argv.index("--")
        argv, o["extra"] = argv[:i], argv[i + 1:]
    names = {"--against": "against", "--canary": "canary", "--json": "json", "--host": "host",
             "--passes-build": "passes_build", "--against-passes-build": "against_passes_build"}
    takes = {"--size", "--frames", "--runs", "--rest", "--canary-share", "--timeout"} | set(names)
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a in ("-h", "--help"):
            raise Usage(__doc__)
        if a == "--no-passes":
            o["passes"] = False
            i += 1
            continue
        if a in takes:
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                raise Usage(f"{a} takes a value")
            v = argv[i + 1]
            i += 2
            try:
                if a == "--size":
                    w, h = v.split("x")
                    assert int(w) > 0 and int(h) > 0
                    o["size"] = v
                elif a == "--frames":
                    lo, hi = v.split("-")
                    o["frames"] = (int(lo), int(hi))
                    assert 0 <= o["frames"][0] <= o["frames"][1]
                elif a == "--runs":
                    o["runs"] = int(v)
                    assert o["runs"] >= 1
                elif a == "--rest":
                    o["rest"] = float(v)
                    assert o["rest"] >= 0
                elif a == "--canary-share":
                    o["share"] = float(v)
                    assert o["share"] >= 0
                elif a == "--timeout":
                    o["timeout"] = float(v)
                    assert o["timeout"] > 0
                else:
                    o[names[a]] = v
            except (ValueError, AssertionError):
                raise Usage(f"{a} doesn't take `{v}`")
        elif a.startswith("-"):
            raise Usage(f"unknown option {a} (wrela-host's own go after `--`)")
        elif o["build"] is None:
            o["build"] = a
            i += 1
        else:
            raise Usage(f"unexpected argument {a}")
    if o["build"] is None:
        raise Usage("which build?")
    for flag in o["extra"]:
        if flag in OWN:
            raise Usage(f"the bench sets {flag} itself" if flag in ("--frames", "--size",
                        "--timestamps", "--serial") else f"{flag} doesn't time frames")
    if o["against_passes_build"] and not o["against"]:
        raise Usage("--against-passes-build goes with --against")
    for b in (o["build"], o["against"], o["passes_build"], o["against_passes_build"]):
        if b is not None and not os.path.isdir(b):
            raise Usage(f"{b} isn't a directory")
    if o["runs"] is None:
        o["runs"] = 3 if o["against"] else 1
    return o


def main(argv):
    if hasattr(sys.stdout, "reconfigure"):
        sys.stdout.reconfigure(line_buffering=True)
    try:
        o = parse_args(argv)
    except Usage as e:
        if str(e) == __doc__:
            print(__doc__, file=sys.stderr)
        else:
            usage = "\n".join(__doc__.splitlines()[2:6])
            print(f"bench: {e}\n{usage}\n(tools/bench --help for more)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    first, last = o["frames"]
    wanted = last - first + 1
    builds = {"A": o["build"]}
    passes = {"A": o["passes_build"] or o["build"]}
    if o["against"]:
        builds["B"] = o["against"]
        passes["B"] = o["against_passes_build"] or o["against"]
    plan = [("span", s) for _ in range(o["runs"]) for s in builds]
    if o["passes"]:
        plan += [("passes", s) for s in builds]
    what = f"{o['build']} against {o['against']}" if o["against"] else o["build"]
    print(f"bench: {what} at {o['size']}, frames {first}-{last}; "
          f"{o['runs']} span {'pair' if o['against'] else 'run'}{'s' if o['runs'] > 1 else ''}"
          f"{', then passes alone' if o['passes'] else ''}"
          f"{(', ' + format(o['rest'], 'g') + ' s rest between runs') if len(plan) > 1 else ''}")
    warnings, began = [], time.monotonic()
    spans = {"A": [], "B": []}      # each span run: {"values", "pieces" (measure), ...}
    tables = {}
    record = {"span_runs": [], "passes_runs": []}
    warned = set()
    for n, (kind, s) in enumerate(plan):
        if n and o["rest"]:
            print(f"bench: resting {o['rest']:g} s", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
            time.sleep(o["rest"])
        wait_quiet()
        build = builds[s] if kind == "span" else passes[s]
        k = len(spans[s]) + 1
        label = ((f"{s} " if o["against"] else "") + (f"run {k}" if kind == "span" else "passes"))
        print(f"bench: {label}: {build}" + (" (passes alone)" if kind == "passes" else ""),
              file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        status, timed, state, waited, took, busy, top = run_once(
            build, o["size"], last, o["extra"], o["host"], o["timeout"], kind == "passes")
        if status != 0:
            print(f"bench: {label} failed (exit {status})", file=sys.stderr)
            return status
        frames, order = read_timings(timed)
        m = measure(frames, order, first, last)
        tail = f"; ran {took - waited:.1f} s ({(took - waited) / (last + 1) * 1000:.0f} ms a frame)"
        if waited:
            tail += f" after {waited:.1f} s waiting for the GPU"
        if busy is not None:
            tail += f"; others' CPU {busy:.0f}%"
        if top is not None:
            tail += f"; GPU clock at its top {top:.0f}% of the run"
        if state:
            tail += f"; state hash {state}"
        if kind == "span":
            values = window(read_spans(timed), first, last)
            if not values:
                print(f"bench: {label} printed no spans for frames {first}-{last}",
                      file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
            t, settle = spread(values), settling(values)
            spans[s].append({"values": values, "pieces": m, "settle": settle})
            line = (f"{label}: span {t['median']:.3f} ms {fmt_range(t['min'], t['max'])}"
                    f"{' (LOAD INCLUDED)' if m['load'] else ''}, {len(values)} frames read")
            if len(values) < wanted:
                line += f" of {wanted} asked"
            print(line + tail, flush=True)
            if len(values) < wanted:
                warn([f"{label} read {len(values)} frames of the {wanted} asked "
                      f"({first}-{last})"], warnings)
            if busy is not None and busy > BUSY:
                warn([f"{label}: the CPU was busy: other processes used {busy:.0f}% of a core",
                      f"(the median of samples every {SAMPLE_S:g} s), past {BUSY:.0f}%. A span",
                      "holds the GPU's idle time while the CPU works inside a frame, and the GPU",
                      "lowers its clock when frames come slowly: this span may read high.",
                      "Rerun when the machine is quiet."], warnings)
            if top is not None and top < CLOCK_TOP:
                warn([f"{label}: the GPU's clock was at its top level in {top:.0f}% of the run's",
                      f"samples (every {CLOCK_S:g} s), under {CLOCK_TOP:.0f}%: frames this light",
                      "leave the GPU idle between them and it lowers its clock, so this span reads",
                      "high and moves run to run. Compare spans only A/B (--against), or read",
                      "the pass table, which a load keeps at the top clock."], warnings)
            if m["load"] and ("span", build) not in warned:
                warned.add(("span", build))
                load_in_span_warning(build, warnings)
            if settle and not settle["settled"]:
                warn([f"{label} is still settling: take later frames (--frames). The window's "
                      f"first third reads {settle['first']:.3f} ms, its last third "
                      f"{settle['last']:.3f}: {settle['first'] - settle['last']:+.3f} ms, past "
                      f"the noise of {settle['noise']:.3f}"], warnings)
            record["span_runs"].append({
                "side": s, "build": build, "run": k, "frames_read": len(values), "hash": state,
                "waited_s": waited, "ran_s": took - waited, "load_included": m["load"],
                "others_cpu_pct": busy,
                "span": t, "settling": settle, "spans": values, "first_frame": first})
        else:
            if not m["frames"]:
                print(f"bench: {label} printed no timings for frames {first}-{last}",
                      file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
            tables[s] = pass_table(m)
            tables[s + "_load"] = m["load"]
            sm = tables[s][SUM]
            print(f"{label}: sum of passes alone {sm['median']:.3f} ms (not the frame), "
                  f"{len(m['frames'])} frames read{tail}", flush=True)
            if not m["load"] and ("passes", build) not in warned:
                warned.add(("passes", build))
                no_load_warning(build, warnings)
            record["passes_runs"].append({
                "side": s, "build": build, "frames_read": len(m["frames"]), "hash": state,
                "waited_s": waited, "ran_s": took - waited, "load": m["load"], "table": tables[s]})
    print()
    result = {"config": dict(o), "warnings": warnings, **record}
    how = ("on the GPU's clock, first pass's start to last pass's end: passes overlapped, "
           "frames back to back")
    if not o["against"]:
        sm = summarize([r["values"] for r in spans["A"]])
        loaded = any(r["pieces"]["load"] for r in spans["A"])
        line = f"{SPAN_NAME}: {sm['median']:.3f} ms "
        if o["runs"] > 1:
            line += f"(the median of {o['runs']} runs' medians), runs {fmt_range(sm['runs_min'], sm['runs_max'])}, "
        line += f"frames {fmt_range(sm['frames_min'], sm['frames_max'])}, {sm['frames']} frames"
        print(line + (" -- LOAD INCLUDED" if loaded else ""))
        print(f"  ({how})")
        result["summary"] = sm
    else:
        a = summarize([r["values"] for r in spans["A"]])
        b = summarize([r["values"] for r in spans["B"]])
        for i, (ra, rb) in enumerate(zip(spans["A"], spans["B"]), 1):
            ma, mb = statistics.median(ra["values"]), statistics.median(rb["values"])
            print(f"pair {i}: A {ma:.3f} ms, B {mb:.3f} ms ({pct(mb - ma, ma)})")
        diff, noise, word = verdict(a["runs"], b["runs"])
        loaded = [s for s in "AB" if any(r["pieces"]["load"] for r in spans[s])]
        print(f"{SPAN_NAME}: {a['median']:.3f} ms {fmt_range(a['runs_min'], a['runs_max'])} -> "
              f"{b['median']:.3f} ms {fmt_range(b['runs_min'], b['runs_max'])}; {diff:+.3f} ms "
              f"({pct(diff, a['median'])}), noise "
              f"{(format(noise, '.3f') + ' ms') if noise is not None else 'unknown'}: "
              f"{word.upper()}" + (f" -- LOAD INCLUDED in {' and '.join(loaded)}" if loaded else ""))
        print(f"  ({how})")
        result["A"], result["B"] = a, b
        result["verdict"] = {"diff": diff, "noise": noise, "verdict": word}
    unsettled = [r for s in "AB" for r in spans[s] if r["settle"] and not r["settle"]["settled"]]
    checked = [r for s in "AB" for r in spans[s] if r["settle"]]
    if checked:
        print(f"settling: {len(checked) - len(unsettled)} of {len(checked)} span run"
              f"{'s' if len(checked) > 1 else ''} settled (first third against last third)"
              + ("" if not unsettled else " -- STILL SETTLING: take later frames"))
    if o["canary"]:
        every = [r["pieces"] for r in spans["A"] + spans["B"]]
        meds, moved, problem = canary_check(every, o["canary"], o["share"])
        if problem:
            warn([problem], warnings)
        elif moved is not None and len(meds) > 1:
            print(f"canary `{o['canary']}`: {min(meds):.3f} to {max(meds):.3f} ms across the span "
                  f"runs, moved {moved:.1f}%, within {o['share']:g}%")
        else:
            print(f"canary `{o['canary']}`: one run, nothing to compare")
        result["canary"] = {"label": o["canary"], "runs": meds, "moved_pct": moved,
                            "share": o["share"], "warning": problem}
    if tables:
        print()
        if o["against"]:
            print_passes_ab(tables["A"], tables["B"], tables["A_load"], tables["B_load"])
        else:
            print_passes(tables["A"], tables["A_load"])
    print(f"bench: {len(plan)} run{'s' if len(plan) > 1 else ''} in "
          f"{time.monotonic() - began:.0f} s", file=sys.stderr)
    if warnings:
        print(f"bench: {len(warnings)} warning{'s' if len(warnings) > 1 else ''}: see above",
              file=sys.stderr)
    if o["json"]:
        with open(o["json"], "w") as f:
            json.dump(result, f, indent=1)
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
